      "message": "Are we *certain* that it doesn\u0027t matter?\n\nWhat happens if someone repeatedly calls rand_bytes() on the same buffer, thus repeatedly re-encrypting the data using new counter values and the same nonce?  Are we certain that doing so will give as statistically-random a set of values, as the normal AES-DRBG approach of encrypting a constant?  Any risk we\u0027ll introduce some subtle correlations, of the same order as the biases that this approach is seeking to eliminate?\n\nI wonder if it\u0027s a more security-conservative thing to do, to memset() the supplied buffer to zeros prior to encrypting?  That\u0027s the well-studied approach for such DRBGs, as far as I know.",
